From 893e0a4b859a1932d729c5abb6d67b8b4410af4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri John Ledkov <dimitri.ledkov@surgut.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:19:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Chainguard Cryptographic Hardening

Unregister weak, inscure, deprecated, broken algorithms from the
default provider. All of these are unused, not part of the FIPS
provider, deprecated by IETF and IANA.

This is done at the provider level, to otherwise keep stable and
compatible ABI and API.
---
